{"authors": [], "discovered_at": "2026-10-31T02:13:51.854555Z", "id": "github:release:535360445:release:429383005", "kind": "release", "matched_terms": [], "metadata": {"action": "released", "draft": false, "forks": 11941, "prerelease": false, "stars": 62991, "stars_delta": 17, "tag_name": "v8.4.194"}, "organization": "ultralytics", "priority": {"source": 0.5}, "published_at": "2026-10-30T18:54:49Z", "related_items": [], "scores": {}, "source": "github", "source_id": "535360445:release:429383005", "summary": "## \ud83c\udf1f Summary\nUltralytics **8.4.194** makes automatic batch sizing more reliable across tasks, alongside practical fixes for model loading, results saving, datasets, and deployment workflows.\n\n## \ud83d\udcca Key Changes\n- \ud83d\ude80 **Automatic batch sizing now uses the training dataset for every task.** It accounts for dataset size and labels across classification, detection, and multi-dataset training. If profiling runs out of memory during backward computation, AutoBatch treats that as a limit rather than relying on an invalid measurement.\n- \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f **Model YAML parsing is safer and more consistent.** Activations must resolve to supported `torch.nn` modules, and model entries must be PyTorch module classes. Custom YAMLs using other expressions may need updating.\n- \ud83d\udcbe **Saving prediction results is more robust.** `Results.save()` and `plot(save=True)` now produce sensible `.jpg` filenames for sources such as webcams, videos, or missing paths, and create parent directories when needed.\n- \ud83d\udd04 **Similarity search uses the selected image directory on each startup.** This avoids reusing stale indexes from another dataset; the trade-off is that embeddings are rebuilt each time.\n- \ud83e\udde9 **Dataset and URL handling is more dependable.** Non-PNG semantic masks are resolved before cache hashing, and URL schemes such as `HTTPS://`, `GS://`, and `UL://` are now handled without case sensitivity.\n- \ud83d\udcc8 **Benchmarking and evaluation guidance are clearer.** TensorFlow GraphDef benchmarks now include OBB and pose, and the docs explain that classes absent from validation receive the overall mAP value rather than a measured per-class score.\n\n## \ud83c\udfaf Purpose & Impact\n- \u2705 AutoBatch is less likely to choose a batch size that exceeds a small dataset or available GPU memory, and multi-dataset World/YOLOE training avoids label-access failures.\n- \ud83d\udd12 Consistent, restricted YAML parsing improves safety, though nonstandard custom model configurations may no longer load.\n- \ud83e\uddf0 More reliable result saving, mask-cache updates, and URL routing reduce common workflow errors.\n- \ud83d\udd0d Similarity search results better reflect the images currently in the chosen folder, while requiring index-building work at startup.\n- \ud83d\udcda Documentation updates clarify metric interpretation and integration behavior; no new model architecture is introduced in this release.\n\n## What's Changed\n* Fix classification dataset URL scheme handling by @Vaishnavi220506 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26879\n* Benchmark TensorFlow GraphDef for OBB and pose by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26952\n* Give each Colab VM its own anonymous settings id by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26959\n* Fix settings help URL punctuation by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26962\n* Update the COCO JSON guide's cache note now that the hash includes mtime by @Echoslayer in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26960\n* Explain how metrics.box.maps fills classes absent from the val set by @Echoslayer in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26955\n* Build the similarity search index from the data directory on every start by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26965\n* Resolve non-PNG semantic mask paths before hashing the label cache by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26954\n* Handle URL schemes case-insensitively at remaining routing sites by @cainiao33 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26964\n* Fix `Results.save` and `plot` default filename when path is None or extensionless by @Rahulbiradar9 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26958\n* Fix stale framing, logger defaults and nav order on integration pages by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26957\n* Use one model YAML parsing path in `parse_model` by @Y-T-G in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26963\n* `ultralytics 8.4.194` Size AutoBatch from the train dataset for every task by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26956\n\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/compare/v8.4.193...v8.4.194\n", "title": "ultralytics/ultralytics v8.4.194 - `ultralytics 8.4.194` Size AutoBatch from the train dataset for every task (#26956)", "topics": ["image_classification", "instance_segmentation", "object_detection", "object_tracking", "semantic_segmentation"], "updated_at": "2026-10-30T18:56:49Z", "url": "https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/releases/tag/v8.4.194", "venue": null}
